WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.568 --> 00:00:14.185
Ascalon is mine again.

2
00:00:16.774 --> 00:00:17.692
And now...

3
00:00:17.796 --> 00:00:20.529
Now you will see what the dragon saw.

4
00:00:29.867 --> 00:00:31.842
Let the dragon come.

5
00:01:02.961 --> 00:01:04.342
I can't believe it.

6
00:01:04.546 --> 00:01:05.224
That.

7
00:01:05.675 --> 00:01:07.428
Who would have thought she had hair like this.

8
00:01:08.084 --> 00:01:10.412
You have my permission to bow.

9
00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:14.029
I will bow when and where I want.

10
00:01:14.675 --> 00:01:17.404
Kevin, "to bow" means yes 
you kneel in front of him.

11
00:01:18.218 --> 00:01:18.857
Oh.

12
00:01:19.355 --> 00:01:21.053
That's not gonna happen, dude.

13
00:01:23.623 --> 00:01:25.615
You must put down the sword!

14
00:01:27.382 --> 00:01:29.670
why would i do that 
young Mr Tennyson?

15
00:01:30.006 --> 00:01:31.615
Askalon is mine.

16
00:01:32.443 --> 00:01:33.263
Not.

17
00:01:37.023 --> 00:01:38.240
It's mine.

18
00:01:40.045 --> 00:01:41.045
Azmut?

19
00:01:41.176 --> 00:01:42.896
Is that your sword?

20
00:01:43.052 --> 00:01:44.584
That's what I said, "my".

21
00:01:44.825 --> 00:01:46.349
Follow the action, Tennyson.

22
00:01:47.615 --> 00:01:50.248
I don't have time to chat with you, Azmut.

23
00:01:50.601 --> 00:01:52.068
The monster is hiding in it!

24
00:01:52.314 --> 00:01:53.568
But not for long.

25
00:01:53.974 --> 00:01:56.420
Now this is over!

26
00:01:59.151 --> 00:02:00.568
Aah!

27
00:02:18.294 --> 00:02:20.709
It was a very silent monster.

28
00:02:21.111 --> 00:02:22.537
It wasn't there.

29
00:02:23.342 --> 00:02:25.881
It seems that when the seal is broken, 
the creature is able

30
00:02:25.906 --> 00:02:28.693
to enter and exit this 
dimensions whenever he wants.

31
00:02:29.108 --> 00:02:31.826
Then we have no reason to 
we drag on with this craziness.

32
00:02:31.851 --> 00:02:32.967
Give me my sword.

33
00:02:33.444 --> 00:02:35.287
Not while Dagon lives.

34
00:02:35.959 --> 00:02:38.209
If you want it, you'll have to get it yourself.

35
00:02:38.521 --> 00:02:39.763
You think I can't?

36
00:02:39.924 --> 00:02:42.912
I am Azmut, creator of the Omnitrix!

37
00:02:42.937 --> 00:02:44.513
Sculptor of worlds!

38
00:02:44.538 --> 00:02:47.224
The smartest being in the five galaxies!

39
00:02:47.249 --> 00:02:49.076
Of course I can take it from you.

40
00:02:50.341 --> 00:02:51.842
Ben Tennyson, take my sword.

41
00:02:52.288 --> 00:02:53.381
All right!

42
00:02:53.584 --> 00:02:54.373
Ben, wait.

43
00:02:54.398 --> 00:02:55.607
Doesn't this seem a little--

44
00:02:55.670 --> 00:02:57.537
Azmut told me to fight.

45
00:02:57.807 --> 00:02:59.209
There's no way I'm going to miss this.

46
00:03:15.364 --> 00:03:16.888
Fast track!

47
00:03:21.568 --> 00:03:23.318
I thought this would go differently.

48
00:03:23.807 --> 00:03:25.185
Not. It's good.

49
00:03:25.443 --> 00:03:27.935
Loses faster than XLR8.

50
00:03:28.605 --> 00:03:30.084
I'm warning you.

51
00:03:47.284 --> 00:03:47.943
What?!

52
00:03:48.275 --> 00:03:50.076
Let...me!

53
00:03:50.455 --> 00:03:51.896
Make me, old man!

54
00:03:55.636 --> 00:03:57.951
Respect your elders, young man.

55
00:03:58.269 --> 00:03:59.318
And besides...

56
00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:00.881
are you pulling your hair?

57
00:04:01.301 --> 00:04:02.256
Seriously?

58
00:04:02.987 --> 00:04:04.795
You fight like a girl.

59
00:04:06.159 --> 00:04:06.959
Wrong.

60
00:04:07.168 --> 00:04:08.654
I fight like a girl!

61
00:04:11.347 --> 00:04:11.998
Huh?

62
00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:14.076
Ugh!

63
00:04:14.903 --> 00:04:16.662
And that should be--

64
00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:22.732
Humongosaurus!

65
00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:44.263
You'll have to do better...

66
00:04:44.745 --> 00:04:45.849
of that!

67
00:04:54.950 --> 00:04:56.631
Well, that didn't go very well.

68
00:04:57.115 --> 00:04:58.857
I was soft on you.

69
00:04:59.157 --> 00:05:00.279
Stay down.

70
00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:02.843
As if that was going to happen.

71
00:05:03.304 --> 00:05:04.562
You have been warned.

72
00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:16.741
It would be very dishonorable of me to give you 
destroy when you don't know what's at stake...

73
00:05:18.115 --> 00:05:20.366
To say nothing of the true power of the sword.

74
00:05:23.285 --> 00:05:28.445
But I assure you, the next time we 
you find yourself on the road, it will be your last.

75
00:05:31.295 --> 00:05:33.390
The man told a compelling story.

76
00:05:33.592 --> 00:05:34.812
What do you think about that, Ben?

77
00:05:36.161 --> 00:05:37.453
Ben is there.

78
00:05:37.675 --> 00:05:38.187
Oh.

79
00:05:38.369 --> 00:05:40.062
I'm half blind, okay?

80
00:05:40.450 --> 00:05:42.273
So I only look half like a man?

81
00:05:43.385 --> 00:05:45.882
Azmut, what was George talking about?

82
00:05:46.234 --> 00:05:48.359
I don't have time for questions.

83
00:05:48.565 --> 00:05:50.784
Actually, I think it is 
the perfect time to test

84
00:05:50.808 --> 00:05:53.440
when someone doesn't beat me 
with a magic sword.

85
00:05:53.757 --> 00:05:54.945
It's not magic.

86
00:05:54.970 --> 00:05:55.991
That's science.

87
00:05:56.337 --> 00:05:57.463
Your science.

88
00:05:57.765 --> 00:05:58.429
Yes, but...

89
00:05:58.454 --> 00:05:59.851
Not! There is no "but"!

90
00:05:59.966 --> 00:06:01.249
"But" is for the weak!

91
00:06:01.866 --> 00:06:03.741
No, "but" is for pronunciation.

92
00:06:04.085 --> 00:06:05.007
And for the weak?

93
00:06:05.251 --> 00:06:07.983
It's for the weak to dust them off 
the man with the magic sword.

94
00:06:08.352 --> 00:06:10.202
I told you it wasn't magic!

95
00:06:10.227 --> 00:06:12.116
Are you people learning anything?

96
00:06:12.365 --> 00:06:16.726
Look, you're always the one yelling at me when
I go into battle without thinking,

97
00:06:16.999 --> 00:06:18.773
and without asking the right questions.

98
00:06:18.965 --> 00:06:20.468
That's why I'm asking now.

99
00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:22.124
Don't I deserve to know?

100
00:06:25.655 --> 00:06:26.624
Good.

101
00:06:27.176 --> 00:06:28.335
Close your eyes.

102
00:06:33.992 --> 00:06:35.140
Now open it.

103
00:06:39.532 --> 00:06:40.445
A teleporter?

104
00:06:40.793 --> 00:06:41.476
It must be.

105
00:06:41.661 --> 00:06:42.632
But where are we?

106
00:06:46.427 --> 00:06:47.648
Gwen! Shields!

107
00:06:48.623 --> 00:06:49.749
Nothing happened!

108
00:06:50.022 --> 00:06:50.820
I can't--

109
00:06:51.038 --> 00:06:51.960
Watch out!

110
00:07:13.924 --> 00:07:15.273
I can't even feel it.

111
00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:17.515
That's because it's not really here.

112
00:07:17.825 --> 00:07:19.405
Is this...Primus?

113
00:07:19.650 --> 00:07:20.304
That.

114
00:07:20.502 --> 00:07:24.023
The world I created several thousand 
years before you saw him.

115
00:07:24.261 --> 00:07:25.640
Works in progress?

116
00:07:26.166 --> 00:07:28.093
We are all works in progress.

117
00:07:28.343 --> 00:07:31.085
You see the images that I implanted in you,

118
00:07:31.124 --> 00:07:33.772
but you are like ghosts 
you can't interfere.

119
00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:37.718
Maybe the concept is too complicated 
for the human brain to understand it.

120
00:07:38.037 --> 00:07:39.780
Not if you've seen the movie "A Christmas Story."

121
00:07:40.019 --> 00:07:42.163
I have no idea what you're talking about.

122
00:07:42.188 --> 00:07:43.952
Now, shut up and pay attention.

123
00:07:44.458 --> 00:07:45.780
Bah, something.

124
00:07:47.565 --> 00:07:48.726
It was sudden.

125
00:07:49.028 --> 00:07:50.030
Really.

126
00:07:50.287 --> 00:07:51.609
Hey! Azmut!

127
00:07:53.379 --> 00:07:54.070
Huh?

128
00:07:56.236 --> 00:07:56.945
Oh.

129
00:07:57.132 --> 00:07:59.265
He is a ghost from Azmut's past.

130
00:07:59.632 --> 00:08:00.484
Yes.

131
00:08:00.695 --> 00:08:04.499
And you can't change the past, 
no matter how much he would like it.

132
00:08:05.133 --> 00:08:05.843
Would you?

133
00:08:06.376 --> 00:08:07.429
I mean, if you could.

134
00:08:08.730 --> 00:08:10.046
Still working, Azmut?

135
00:08:10.544 --> 00:08:12.804
If I knew you would become 
so obsessed with it

136
00:08:12.918 --> 00:08:15.874
she would never make you that one 
subatomic browser.

137
00:08:16.507 --> 00:08:20.093
It allows us to see 
to the primal power of the universe, Zenith!

138
00:08:20.406 --> 00:08:22.288
How can you not want to use it?

139
00:08:22.674 --> 00:08:24.398
We've talked about this before.

140
00:08:24.589 --> 00:08:27.484
And you promised me an evening outside the lab.

141
00:08:29.085 --> 00:08:30.218
You're right, love.

142
00:08:30.981 --> 00:08:32.077
Seriously?

143
00:08:32.353 --> 00:08:33.554
I think that's really cute.

144
00:08:34.108 --> 00:08:35.187
Well, she was.

145
00:08:36.077 --> 00:08:37.499
She was pure perfection.

146
00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:43.046
Zenit, how can you not see the possibility 
penetration into the fundamental forces?

147
00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:45.780
I'm just as interested in those forces as you are,

148
00:08:46.090 --> 00:08:48.874
but I don't see the need to control everything.

149
00:08:49.343 --> 00:08:52.991
If you can't control something, 
then you don't really understand him.

150
00:08:53.389 --> 00:08:57.905
I understand you, Azmut,
and I'm sure you're out of control.

151
00:09:00.594 --> 00:09:01.577
All right, Zenit.

152
00:09:02.208 --> 00:09:03.624
I'll try your way.

153
00:09:04.273 --> 00:09:05.007
I promise.

154
00:09:05.834 --> 00:09:08.359
Let me guess -- you broke your promise.

155
00:09:08.662 --> 00:09:11.241
I really tried to 
do as she asked

156
00:09:11.537 --> 00:09:14.116
but Zenit is for me then 
turned her attention to something.

157
00:09:14.796 --> 00:09:15.757
Look, Azmut.

158
00:09:16.122 --> 00:09:18.734
That planetary system is 
in perfect syzygy.

159
00:09:19.198 --> 00:09:20.054
Perfect what?

160
00:09:20.196 --> 00:09:22.615
That means alignment -- all in one line.

161
00:09:22.903 --> 00:09:23.673
Yes.

162
00:09:23.923 --> 00:09:28.127
And then I looked up at the sky, 
staring at those bright planets,

163
00:09:28.152 --> 00:09:32.346
how they sparkle in a straight line, 
and all i could see was...

164
00:09:33.307 --> 00:09:34.487
A sword?

165
00:09:35.667 --> 00:09:36.642
It's perfect!

166
00:09:36.823 --> 00:09:40.400
He could break through reality, 
to penetrate the primary energy.

167
00:09:40.765 --> 00:09:45.111
It is very irresponsible to create things 
without thinking about the consequences.

168
00:09:45.492 --> 00:09:47.986
It's not my job to worry 
what will happen next.

169
00:09:48.223 --> 00:09:50.486
What matters is what happens now.

170
00:09:51.949 --> 00:09:53.189
Well, that's true.

171
00:09:53.411 --> 00:09:54.423
Oh! What?!

172
00:09:54.578 --> 00:09:56.104
No, it's not true!

173
00:09:56.129 --> 00:09:58.213
That's what I'm trying to explain to you!

174
00:09:58.426 --> 00:10:02.267
If I was once young and stupid, 
as you are right now!

175
00:10:11.978 --> 00:10:12.687
Zenith!

176
00:10:12.826 --> 00:10:13.983
It's finally over!

177
00:10:14.008 --> 00:10:14.897
Come and see!

178
00:10:16.495 --> 00:10:17.226
Zenith?

179
00:10:18.750 --> 00:10:20.116
Ah, good. He'll be back.

180
00:10:22.123 --> 00:10:23.983
But she didn't come back, did she?

181
00:10:24.564 --> 00:10:25.171
Not.

182
00:10:25.800 --> 00:10:28.499
That, Ben Tennyson, was the point.

183
00:10:28.783 --> 00:10:30.401
So you hit me in the head because you are you

184
00:10:30.426 --> 00:10:32.487
you were too stupid 
ignored your girlfriend?

185
00:10:32.708 --> 00:10:34.554
When was the last time you called Julie?

186
00:10:34.824 --> 00:10:35.944
This is not about me.

187
00:10:36.192 --> 00:10:36.866
Not?

188
00:10:37.810 --> 00:10:39.093
What happened to the sword?

189
00:10:39.303 --> 00:10:40.874
Heard of the Incursions?

190
00:10:41.216 --> 00:10:41.812
Of course.

191
00:10:41.837 --> 00:10:46.319
Warriors who go through space and always fight
against each other and with everyone else.

192
00:10:46.682 --> 00:10:49.569
Have you ever wondered what 
what happened to their homeworld?

193
00:10:50.652 --> 00:10:56.226
It was ravaged by war, multiple factions 
fought in an eons-long civil war.

194
00:10:56.960 --> 00:11:00.585
But one that was meant to be 
the hero heard of my sword, stole it,

195
00:11:00.610 --> 00:11:05.155
and brought it back home, he wanted to use it 
his power to unite his world.

196
00:11:06.142 --> 00:11:07.710
This was the result.

197
00:11:22.723 --> 00:11:23.913
What did I do?

198
00:11:26.237 --> 00:11:27.968
In the end, Zenit was right.

199
00:11:28.482 --> 00:11:33.304
I swore to hide the sword and 
to devote his life to peaceful science.

200
00:11:33.599 --> 00:11:37.569
And you created the Omnitrix as a way to 
you promote interstellar peace and unity.

201
00:11:37.892 --> 00:11:41.147
It was an apology of sorts 
for what I had previously created.

202
00:11:41.422 --> 00:11:43.015
And I turned it into a weapon.

203
00:11:43.919 --> 00:11:45.397
Funny how it turned out, huh?

204
00:11:45.779 --> 00:11:47.733
Yes. Hilarious.

205
00:11:48.024 --> 00:11:48.960
I don't understand.

206
00:11:49.099 --> 00:11:51.179
How did George end up with the sword?

207
00:11:51.695 --> 00:11:53.155
I gave it to him.

208
00:11:59.526 --> 00:12:00.999
That doesn't sound good.

209
00:12:01.247 --> 00:12:02.280
Where are we now?

210
00:12:02.607 --> 00:12:06.476
Pathetic remote planet
which I came across in my studies.

211
00:12:06.932 --> 00:12:08.085
It's Earth, isn't it?

212
00:12:08.412 --> 00:12:09.116
Yes.

213
00:12:09.416 --> 00:12:12.611
I came here when the history of the earth 
was in its darkest period,

214
00:12:13.190 --> 00:12:15.228
 and I only made things worse.

215
00:12:19.669 --> 00:12:22.434
The creature tried to cross
dimensions and to return

216
00:12:22.459 --> 00:12:25.450
 here in, how are you 
called, the Middle Ages.

217
00:12:28.691 --> 00:12:31.824
His subjects, already in ours 
dimensions to pave the way

218
00:12:31.849 --> 00:12:32.870
have come across...

219
00:12:33.135 --> 00:12:34.347
resistance.

220
00:12:36.609 --> 00:12:38.937
The Knights performed well,

221
00:12:39.007 --> 00:12:42.444
but many have fallen on
the mind control powers of those creatures.

222
00:12:48.894 --> 00:12:51.157
So knight turned against knight.

223
00:12:52.710 --> 00:12:58.860
Only the strongest managed to defend themselves,
and the strongest of all, was Sir George.

224
00:14:12.625 --> 00:14:15.243
No matter how brave he was, he too would fall

225
00:14:15.268 --> 00:14:17.829
if I hadn't...interfered.

226
00:14:23.189 --> 00:14:24.134
A rough day?

227
00:14:27.439 --> 00:14:29.056
Demon from the Pit!

228
00:14:29.598 --> 00:14:30.946
Little demon.

229
00:14:31.237 --> 00:14:32.774
I am not a demon from the pit.

230
00:14:33.081 --> 00:14:34.853
I am a visitor from the stars.

231
00:14:35.176 --> 00:14:37.540
Not everyone is who they say they are.

232
00:14:37.945 --> 00:14:38.954
You should know.

233
00:14:39.308 --> 00:14:41.243
You are more than what you show, aren't you?

234
00:14:41.741 --> 00:14:44.579
You were born when...
900 earth years ago?

235
00:14:45.046 --> 00:14:47.970
- How are you--
- My job is to know.

236
00:14:49.152 --> 00:14:50.064
It's true.

237
00:14:50.216 --> 00:14:54.689
I was born George, 
Roman soldier in the year 231 AD.

238
00:14:54.925 --> 00:14:56.298
almost a whole millennium ago.

239
00:14:56.846 --> 00:14:59.079
And how, that's a story for another day.

240
00:14:59.297 --> 00:15:01.751
It would have been better if I hadn't been 
blessed with immortality

241
00:15:01.776 --> 00:15:04.462
not to see humanity 
how does it fall this low.

242
00:15:05.087 --> 00:15:07.675
We don't have a weapon that can 
to defeat the creatures.

243
00:15:07.908 --> 00:15:09.073
Now you have.

244
00:15:11.773 --> 00:15:14.277
This sword is a weapon of unprecedented power.

245
00:15:14.561 --> 00:15:18.089
If one who is worthy directs it, 
cannot be stopped.

246
00:15:18.412 --> 00:15:21.803
If it's so scary, 
why don't you keep it for yourself?

247
00:15:21.999 --> 00:15:23.646
Because I'm not worthy of it.

248
00:15:35.176 --> 00:15:36.256
Listen to me carefully.

249
00:15:36.634 --> 00:15:39.920
The creatures you are fighting now are not
nothing compared to their master.

250
00:15:40.193 --> 00:15:44.139
He captured hundreds of dimensions and 
now he is looking for a way to capture ours as well.

251
00:15:44.485 --> 00:15:48.607
If he gets a foothold there,
our entire universe will fall.

252
00:15:49.144 --> 00:15:51.959
When Dagon comes, you must destroy him!

253
00:15:52.441 --> 00:15:54.607
What will happen after I kill Dagon?

254
00:15:55.230 --> 00:15:57.185
I really don't believe that 
you will be able to do it.

255
00:15:58.308 --> 00:16:00.146
Do not doubt me, wise one.

256
00:16:00.569 --> 00:16:03.029
Your gift may have saved humanity.

257
00:16:07.567 --> 00:16:10.139
Saved him or destroyed him.

258
00:16:10.405 --> 00:16:13.201
After he won
knights errant and lucubres,

259
00:16:13.256 --> 00:16:15.756
Saint George was left alone against Dagon.

260
00:16:16.357 --> 00:16:19.615
He cut out the creature's heart 
and left the sword in it.

261
00:16:19.961 --> 00:16:20.889
I'll show you.

262
00:16:27.913 --> 00:16:28.709
No.

263
00:16:28.954 --> 00:16:29.467
I...

264
00:16:30.195 --> 00:16:31.318
I can't watch.

265
00:16:31.808 --> 00:16:32.990
I'm going to be sick.

266
00:16:33.437 --> 00:16:35.349
Azmut, get us out of here now!

267
00:16:35.561 --> 00:16:36.334
Now!

268
00:16:36.677 --> 00:16:37.912
As you wish.

269
00:16:40.215 --> 00:16:41.233
are you ok

270
00:16:41.574 --> 00:16:42.702
It was horrible.

271
00:16:43.367 --> 00:16:44.141
It was--

272
00:16:44.598 --> 00:16:46.632
We don't need to be involved in this.

273
00:16:47.062 --> 00:16:50.796
Why stop George at all if
wants to use the sword to kill the monster?

274
00:16:51.091 --> 00:16:54.624
Because the monster won't 
underestimate the second time.

275
00:16:55.284 --> 00:17:00.655
George will probably never hit the target,
and meanwhile the power of the sword will overcome him.

276
00:17:01.107 --> 00:17:03.929
Your world can be transformed 
into floating ruins.

277
00:17:04.429 --> 00:17:05.061
Good.

278
00:17:05.086 --> 00:17:07.405
So you say that the sword is needed 
to be used by someone worthy,

279
00:17:07.873 --> 00:17:09.929
someone who is incredibly brave and handsome…

280
00:17:10.428 --> 00:17:12.577
someone with a stylized green jacket.

281
00:17:12.901 --> 00:17:14.530
Did you learn something?

282
00:17:14.849 --> 00:17:17.147
The power of the sword will defeat you too!

283
00:17:17.468 --> 00:17:19.726
Haven't you learned anything for
the past six years?

284
00:17:19.938 --> 00:17:22.015
I'm the right man for 
saving the universe!

285
00:17:22.395 --> 00:17:24.030
We don't even know where he is!

286
00:17:24.197 --> 00:17:27.015
I think I have something that belonged to him, 
maybe I could find him.

287
00:17:27.341 --> 00:17:28.694
How about this?

288
00:17:30.905 --> 00:17:32.897
What is that? His hair?

289
00:17:33.290 --> 00:17:33.937
That.

290
00:17:34.022 --> 00:17:35.913
She snapped when he threw me off him.

291
00:17:36.011 --> 00:17:37.788
Be careful, Ben Tennyson.

292
00:17:37.987 --> 00:17:40.140
Now you know what's at stake.

293
00:17:40.492 --> 00:17:40.890
Hey.

294
00:17:40.915 --> 00:17:44.171
I don't even bother to get up
out of bed if the universe is not in danger.

295
00:17:46.639 --> 00:17:48.187
He's in Area 51.

296
00:17:48.448 --> 00:17:49.647
Rock and roll.

297
00:18:05.621 --> 00:18:06.202
Huh?

298
00:18:13.178 --> 00:18:14.640
It never gets old.

299
00:18:26.935 --> 00:18:27.819
There they are!

300
00:18:40.353 --> 00:18:41.515
Good night.

301
00:18:45.768 --> 00:18:47.226
So predictable.

302
00:18:47.783 --> 00:18:49.187
Tell me, Lord Tennyson,

303
00:18:49.546 --> 00:18:53.671
how can you think that you, who has yet to 
to live a lifetime,

304
00:18:53.944 --> 00:18:56.929
you can know better than me 
who lived thousands?

305
00:18:57.205 --> 00:18:59.164
Azmut lived much more than that.

306
00:18:59.460 --> 00:19:00.375
That.

307
00:19:00.589 --> 00:19:02.867
And did you notice that he is not here?

308
00:19:02.973 --> 00:19:03.601
That.

309
00:19:03.626 --> 00:19:04.898
But guess who it is.

310
00:19:06.496 --> 00:19:09.015
Humongosaurus!

311
00:19:11.076 --> 00:19:14.304
The ultimate Humongosaur!

312
00:19:14.808 --> 00:19:15.554
You are big.

313
00:19:15.929 --> 00:19:17.351
But I also killed bigger ones.

314
00:19:36.076 --> 00:19:38.656
That sword has too much power for you!

315
00:19:38.942 --> 00:19:40.211
Azmut says...

316
00:19:40.699 --> 00:19:42.414
Oh, "Azmut says."

317
00:19:42.788 --> 00:19:45.420
People questioned you, 
lord Tennyson,

318
00:19:45.685 --> 00:19:47.764
all from Azmut, through your parents

319
00:19:47.850 --> 00:19:49.586
to those vultures from the media.

320
00:19:49.869 --> 00:19:53.171
Don't you get frustrated by what they think? 
that they know better than you?

321
00:19:54.153 --> 00:19:56.476
A little, yes.

322
00:19:56.753 --> 00:19:58.687
Welcome to my world.

323
00:20:13.245 --> 00:20:18.406
It doesn't matter what you think,
sooner or later the sword will corrupt you!

324
00:20:20.457 --> 00:20:21.757
Not earlier.

325
00:20:21.867 --> 00:20:23.750
I have achieved great things with him.

326
00:20:24.045 --> 00:20:25.695
My works are legendary.

327
00:20:25.992 --> 00:20:27.445
They are mine too!

328
00:20:28.064 --> 00:20:30.250
But mine have stood the test of time.

329
00:20:30.530 --> 00:20:32.304
Mine have inspired millions.

330
00:20:32.484 --> 00:20:33.992
What will your legacy be?

331
00:20:34.341 --> 00:20:36.453
Which stars will you enter into an alliance with?

332
00:20:37.021 --> 00:20:41.234
How many times have you known in your heart 
that your way is best?

333
00:20:41.534 --> 00:20:43.725
How many times have your plans been thwarted

334
00:20:43.764 --> 00:20:46.834
because those very people to whom 
you tried to help, they didn't believe you?

335
00:20:50.031 --> 00:20:51.319
What do you want?

336
00:20:51.459 --> 00:20:55.709
To leave me alone so I could
to destroy my ancient enemy.

337
00:20:57.740 --> 00:20:58.498
Good.

338
00:20:58.644 --> 00:21:00.162
My friends and I will retire.

339
00:21:00.640 --> 00:21:03.904
But when you fail, the sword is mine.

340
00:21:07.960 --> 00:21:10.522
So we risked our lives for nothing.

341
00:21:10.666 --> 00:21:11.256
No.

342
00:21:11.691 --> 00:21:13.967
This way we have two chances to destroy it...

343
00:21:14.283 --> 00:21:15.311
whatever it is.

344
00:21:15.483 --> 00:21:17.662
George earned the right 
to try it his way.

345
00:21:18.008 --> 00:21:20.803
Azmut, I don't think you should have 
that you are trying to stop him.

346
00:21:21.129 --> 00:21:22.233
You might be right.

347
00:21:22.365 --> 00:21:25.490
I mean, George says I'm like him,
you say i'm like you.

348
00:21:25.717 --> 00:21:27.873
I'm just trying to--
Wait, what?

349
00:21:28.165 --> 00:21:28.920
Am I right?

350
00:21:29.705 --> 00:21:32.053
Maybe the end of the world is really coming.

351
00:21:32.693 --> 00:21:35.022
I said you might be right.

352
00:21:35.343 --> 00:21:38.998
And it's not like I never did 
made mistakes, as you now know.

353
00:21:40.539 --> 00:21:45.967
All the reasons I created 
The Omnitrix and the Ultimatrix -- they are all true.

354
00:21:46.740 --> 00:21:49.873
But there was another -- the real reason.

355
00:21:51.316 --> 00:21:53.709
I was hoping she would notice that.


